'''''[[Strictly Come Dancing]]''''' returned for its '''ninth series''' on 10 September 2011 with a launch show,<ref>[http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s104/strictly-come-dancing/news/a338005/dolly-parton-to-play-strictly-come-dancing-red-carpet-launch.html Dolly Parton to play Strictly Come Dancing red carpet launch]</ref> with the live shows beginning on 30 September and 1 October 2011. The show was broadcast from [[Wembley Arena]] on 19 November with all proceeds going to the BBC charity, [[Children in Need]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/webarchive/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bbc.co.uk%2Fblogs%2Fstrictlycomedancing%2F2011%2F07%2Fstrictly-come-dancing-from-wem.shtml|title=Strictly Come Dancing from Wembley}}</ref> The finale took place in the [[Blackpool Tower#Tower Ballroom|Tower Ballroom]] at the [[Blackpool Tower]] and was the first episode to air in [[3D television|3D]]. It was shown on [[BBC HD]] and in cinemas around the country.<ref>{{cite web|author=BBC Strictly Nora |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/webarchive/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bbc.co.uk%2Fblogs%2Fstrictlycomedancing%2F2011%2F12%2Fthe-strictly-final-live-in-3d.shtml |title=Strictly Come Dancing: The Strictly Final Live in 3D! |publisher=BBC |access-date=22 June 2012}}</ref>

[[Sir Bruce Forsyth]] and [[Tess Daly]] continued to present the main show on [[BBC One]], while the results show was presented by Daly and [[Claudia Winkleman]]. Former contestant [[Zoe Ball]] replaced Winkleman as the regular presenter of the spin-off show ''[[Strictly Come Dancing: It Takes Two]]'' due to Winkleman's family commitments.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.metro.co.uk/tv/868463-zoe-ball-to-present-strictly-come-dancing-spin-off-it-takes-two|title=Zoe Ball to present Strictly Come Dancing spin off It Takes Two|work=Metro}}</ref> [[Alesha Dixon]], [[Len Goodman]], [[Craig Revel Horwood]], and [[Bruno Tonioli]] returned as judges. On 5 and 6 November, [[Jennifer Grey]], the winner of the [[Dancing with the Stars (American season 11)|eleventh series of]] ''[[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series)|Dancing with the Stars]]'', served as a guest judge, replacing Len Goodman for the week.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s104/strictly-come-dancing/news/a346535/dirty-dancing-jennifer-grey-to-guest-judge-strictly-come-dancing.html|title=Dirty Dancing Jennifer Grey to guest judge Strictly Come Dancing|work=Digital Spy}}</ref> This was Alesha Dixon's last series as a judge after three years, which the BBC announced on 2 January 2012; she left the show to serve as a judge on a rival show, ''[[Britain's Got Talent]]''.<ref>{{cite web |date=2 January 2012 |title=Alesha Dixon quits 'Strictly Come Dancing' – Strictly Come Dancing News – Reality TV |url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s104/strictly-come-dancing/news/a357958/alesha-dixon-quits-strictly-come-dancing.html |access-date=22 June 2012 |work=Digital Spy}}</ref>

[[Pasha Kovalev]] joined the cast this series as a new professional dancer.

[[McFly]] drummer [[Harry Judd]] and [[Aliona Vilani]] were announced as the winners on 17 December, while ''[[Waterloo Road (TV series)|Waterloo Road]]'' actress [[Chelsee Healey]] and [[Pasha Kovalev]] finished in second place, and actor [[Jason Donovan]] and [[Kristina Rihanoff]] finished in third.

